00:52:45.190 --> 00:52:50.010
When she got up, we had grabbed paper towels and put it on the pee spot on her chair.
当她站起来时，我们抓起纸巾盖在了她椅子上的尿渍上。

1290
00:52:50.830 --> 00:52:52.110
There wasn't much.
没多少东西。

1291
00:52:52.270 --> 00:52:55.290
There were some little napkins and then like papers.
只有一些小餐巾纸，还有一些纸张。

1292
00:52:55.470 --> 00:52:57.010
We just put it on top.
我们就把它盖在上面。

1293
00:52:57.050 --> 00:52:57.550
Tried to, yeah.
试着，对。

1294
00:52:57.730 --> 00:52:58.150
Dab it.
吸干它。

1295
00:52:58.310 --> 00:52:58.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1296
00:52:59.110 --> 00:52:59.970
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

1297
00:53:00.270 --> 00:53:00.910
Oh my gosh.
我的天啊。

1298
00:53:01.250 --> 00:53:06.050
Well, I remember this too, because I remember we were like, oh my gosh, we're always going
嗯，我也记得这件事，因为我记得我们当时说，天哪，我们永远

1299
00:53:06.050 --> 00:53:09.550
to remember this episode because it's the episode where Ellie peed her pants.
都会记得这一集，因为这就是艾莉尿裤子的那一集。

1300
00:53:09.830 --> 00:53:10.050
Yeah.
没错。

1301
00:53:10.270 --> 00:53:13.370
We thought this was going to be the memorable thing about this episode.
我们原以为这会是本集最令人难忘的事。

1302
00:53:13.630 --> 00:53:16.450
Peed her pants work bus, not death bus.
是尿裤子工作巴士，不是死亡巴士。

1303
00:53:16.670 --> 00:53:19.010
We could not have imagined what was to come.
我们当时根本无法想象接下来会发生什么。

1304
00:53:19.450 --> 00:53:22.350
Thank you, Ellie, so much for sending in your story.
非常感谢艾莉发来你的故事。

1305
00:53:22.350 --> 00:53:22.400
I know, Ellie.
我知道，艾莉。

1306
00:53:22.400 --> 00:53:23.230
That was fantastic.
那真是太棒了。

1307
00:53:23.230 --> 00:53:30.350
I also want to point out, if you watch us during this song, just how very sweaty both
我还想指出一点，如果你在看这首歌的时候，注意一下约翰和布莱恩

1308
00:53:30.350 --> 00:53:32.190
John and Brian are in this scene.
在这场戏里有多么汗流浃背。

1309
00:53:32.550 --> 00:53:33.650
Just note it.
留意一下就行。

1310
00:53:33.770 --> 00:53:34.930
We were so hot.
我们当时太热了。

1311
00:53:35.130 --> 00:53:35.610
So hot.
太热了。

1312
00:53:35.710 --> 00:53:38.470
And the guys had on their blazers and oh, Lord.
而且男士们还穿着西装外套，天哪。

1313
00:53:38.670 --> 00:53:40.410
This was the first time we were comfortable.
这是我们第一次感到舒适。

1314
00:53:41.250 --> 00:53:43.030
I don't recall being hot.
我不记得当时很热。

1315
00:53:43.970 --> 00:53:46.890
I do remember feeling kind of stagnant.
我记得当时感觉空气有点不流通。

1316
00:53:46.890 --> 00:53:47.850
It was stuffy.
很闷。

1317
00:53:47.870 --> 00:53:48.110
It was stagnant.
空气不流通。

1318
00:53:48.330 --> 00:53:48.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1319
00:53:48.810 --> 00:53:48.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1320
00:53:49.190 --> 00:53:49.630
It was.
确实。

1321
00:53:49.830 --> 00:53:50.730
Like no air moving.
就像没有空气流动一样。

1322
00:53:50.990 --> 00:53:51.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1323
00:53:51.390 --> 00:53:51.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1324
00:53:51.870 --> 00:53:54.290
We've got a little one-off joke coming up.
接下来有个小小的插曲笑话。

1325
00:53:54.470 --> 00:53:59.430
Dwight notices a hitchhiker on the side of the road and he goes to pick this person up
德怀特注意到路边有个搭车的人，他准备去接这个人，

1326
00:53:59.430 --> 00:53:59.950
and guess what?
结果你猜怎么着？

1327
00:54:00.030 --> 00:54:00.490
It's Creed.
是克里德。

1328
00:54:00.910 --> 00:54:01.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1329
00:54:01.870 --> 00:54:05.570
Creed's like, turns out he's playing hooky for work.
克里德说，原来他上班在逃课。

1330
00:54:05.730 --> 00:54:08.550
And I thought Creed did such a fantastic job.
我觉得克里德演得太棒了。

1331
00:54:08.710 --> 00:54:11.990
His expression when he sees everyone on the bus was so good.
他看到车上所有人时的表情真是太到位了。

1332
00:54:12.130 --> 00:54:15.790
We're going to have a moment now where the bus is clearly pulled over.
现在我们要进入一个片段，巴士明显停在路边。

1333
00:54:16.090 --> 00:54:19.630
Everyone is posing for a group photo in front of a big rooster.
大家都在一只大公鸡雕像前摆姿势拍合影。

1334
00:54:20.210 --> 00:54:21.070
Location alert.
外景地提醒。

1335
00:54:21.430 --> 00:54:23.750
We filmed these rooster scenes at Woodley Park.
这些公鸡的戏份是在伍德利公园拍的。

1336
00:54:24.010 --> 00:54:27.410
This was actually the same day that we shot all the baseball field stuff.
这其实和我们拍棒球场戏份是同一天。

1337
00:54:28.090 --> 00:54:30.510
This happened on our first day on location.
这是我们第一天在外景地拍摄。

1338
00:54:30.510 --> 00:54:31.730
It was really lovely.
真的很棒。

1339
00:54:32.170 --> 00:54:38.850
We had a beautiful base camp with our trailers and changes of clothes and great lunch.
我们有一个很棒的大本营，有拖车、换衣间和很棒的午餐。

1340
00:54:39.070 --> 00:54:40.190
This was a wonderful day.
这是美好的一天。

1341
00:54:40.410 --> 00:54:44.370
I brought my football because the park was right there so we could toss the ball.
我带了橄榄球，因为公园就在那儿，所以我们可以抛球玩。

1342
00:54:44.550 --> 00:54:45.650
This was a wonderful day.
这是美好的一天。

1343
00:54:45.930 --> 00:54:49.530
But Pam is going to notice that Dwight has kind of wandered off on his own
但帕姆注意到德怀特好像独自走开了，

1344
00:54:49.530 --> 00:54:53.470
and she's kind of planting the seed like, what's going on with Dwight?
她开始埋下伏笔，比如，德怀特怎么了？

1345
00:54:54.130 --> 00:54:59.130
You know, Pam is always pretty attuned to Dwight's, I guess, emotional life.
你知道，帕姆一直对德怀特的，我猜，情感生活相当敏锐。

1346
00:54:59.270 --> 00:55:00.250
She really is.
确实如此。

1347
00:55:00.250 --> 00:55:01.570
She has a soft spot for him.
她对他心存善意。

1348
00:55:01.890 --> 00:55:06.350
Well, now I think it's time for us to have a get-to-know-your-cast-and-crew moment from the call sheet.
好了，现在我觉得是时候从通告单上了解一下我们的演职人员了。

1349
00:55:06.390 --> 00:55:07.270
Oh, all right.
哦，好的。

1350
00:55:07.630 --> 00:55:10.770
This is about John Egott, who worked in special effects.
这位是约翰·埃戈特，他在特效部门工作。

1351
00:55:11.230 --> 00:55:13.370
Three things you didn't know about John.
关于约翰，你不知道的三件事。

1352
00:55:13.650 --> 00:55:16.810
He has too many favorite books and cannot pick just one.
他喜欢的书太多了，选不出最喜欢的一本。

1353
00:55:16.810 --> 00:55:18.850
If it is written, he will read it.
只要是写出来的东西，他都会读。

1354
00:55:19.230 --> 00:55:23.990
The prettiest place he has ever been is Lake Tahoe in the 1960s.
他去过最美的地方是20世纪60年代的太浩湖。

1355
00:55:24.370 --> 00:55:27.810
He was once a DJ in a French bordello.
他曾经在一家法国妓院当过DJ。

1356
00:55:27.810 --> 00:55:32.210
And his favorite midnight snack is cold, Colonel Sanders.
他最喜欢的宵夜是凉的肯德基炸鸡。

1357
00:55:32.610 --> 00:55:33.090
Huh.
哈。

1358
00:55:33.430 --> 00:55:35.350
I think they're adding a new question.
我想他们要加个新问题。

1359
00:55:35.350 --> 00:55:36.950
What's your favorite midnight snack?
你最喜欢的宵夜是什么？

1360
00:55:37.510 --> 00:55:40.350
I'll be adding that the next time we have a gueSt.
下次有嘉宾来的时候，我会加上这个问题。

1361
00:55:40.690 --> 00:55:41.770
Y'all know mine.
你们都知道我最喜欢什么。

1362
00:55:41.770 --> 00:55:44.030
Oh, cereal.
哦，麦片。

1363
00:55:44.270 --> 00:55:45.170
Lucky charMs.
幸运符麦片。

1364
00:55:45.650 --> 00:55:45.790
Yeah.
没错。

1365
00:55:46.130 --> 00:55:48.250
I think that's a great question to ask people.
我觉得这是个问人的好问题。

1366
00:55:48.790 --> 00:55:58.170
You know, Angela, since we've gone off topic here for just a moment, over the break, I started realizing that I'm probably going to get a bunch of, like,
安吉拉，既然我们刚才稍微偏离了主题，休息的时候我开始意识到，我可能会收到一大堆，比如，

1367
00:55:58.250 --> 00:56:03.750
mail from people about my landline 911 paranoia, about knowing my location.
人们关于我担心座机911定位问题的来信，关于知道我位置的问题。

1368
00:56:03.750 --> 00:56:09.770
I feel like people are going to tell me that actually my cell phone can pinpoint my location.
我觉得人们会告诉我，其实我的手机可以精确定位我的位置。

1369
00:56:09.890 --> 00:56:15.990
And I just want everyone to know that I don't turn on my location on my cell phone.
我只想让大家知道，我没有开启手机的定位功能。

1370
00:56:16.130 --> 00:56:19.670
And the reason that I don't do that is very important to me.
我不开启定位的原因对我来说非常重要。

1371
00:56:19.770 --> 00:56:23.230
And it is because I don't want to get framed for a crime.
那就是因为我不想被人陷害去犯罪。

1372
00:56:23.850 --> 00:56:26.410
You don't want to get pinged in the cell phone.
你不想被手机信号定位到。

1373
00:56:26.410 --> 00:56:35.610
Yeah, I don't like the idea that, like, I might get framed one day for a major crime because the location thing was on on my cell phone.
对，我不喜欢那种想法，就是有一天我可能会因为手机开了定位而被陷害犯下重罪。

1374
00:56:36.750 --> 00:56:45.850
And so, you guys, I just need you all to know that I really need that landline because my cell phone is not pinpointing my location.
所以，伙计们，我需要你们知道，我真的需要那部座机，因为我的手机无法精确定位我的位置。

1375
00:56:46.110 --> 00:56:48.550
And now, listen, I don't know if it can still ping.
现在，听着，我不知道它是否还能被定位。

1376
00:56:48.750 --> 00:56:51.070
Like, when you use it, maybe it pings the towers.
比如，当你使用它时，也许它会连接信号塔。

1377
00:56:51.070 --> 00:56:52.530
I'm going to need to look into this.
我得好好研究一下这个问题。

1378
00:56:52.590 --> 00:56:55.350
But my mind has been on fire ever since I brought it up.
但自从我提起这件事以来，我的大脑就一直转个不停。

1379
00:56:55.350 --> 00:56:58.430
My kids just did mock trial at school.
我的孩子们刚在学校参加了模拟法庭。

1380
00:56:58.710 --> 00:56:59.810
You know, they learn a trial.
你知道，他们学习审判流程。

1381
00:56:59.970 --> 00:57:03.030
And then they go in front of a real judge and they try a case.
然后他们会在真正的法官面前审理一个案件。

1382
00:57:03.550 --> 00:57:06.730
And their case, there was a murder in a hotel.
他们的案子是关于酒店里发生的一起谋杀案。

1383
00:57:06.990 --> 00:57:08.570
Did they use the cell phone pings?
他们用了手机定位信号吗？

1384
00:57:08.570 --> 00:57:10.970
The investigators used the cell phone pings.
调查人员使用了手机定位信号。

1385
00:57:11.110 --> 00:57:15.910
And they did a radius that the defense thought was too broad.
他们划定了一个辩方认为范围太广的区域。

1386
00:57:16.750 --> 00:57:25.330
And they contested it and got it expunged so that the jurors never even heard about what cell phones were there.
辩方对此提出异议并将其撤销了，所以陪审员们根本没听说过当时有哪些手机在现场。

1387
00:57:25.350 --> 00:57:28.110
But the radius was really big.
但那个范围真的很大。

1388
00:57:28.370 --> 00:57:32.570
It covered the hotel, the street corner.
它覆盖了酒店和街角。

1389
00:57:32.930 --> 00:57:34.190
Like, it was really big.
真的非常大。

1390
00:57:34.190 --> 00:57:37.610
And they had everyone's cell phone information from that area.
他们掌握了该区域所有人的手机信息。

1391
00:57:37.790 --> 00:57:41.090
Now, I think you have to turn on airplane mode to stop the pings.
现在，我觉得你必须开启飞行模式才能阻止定位信号。

1392
00:57:41.270 --> 00:57:42.510
But then you can't get calls.
但那样你就接不到电话了。

1393
00:57:42.870 --> 00:57:43.370
I know.
我知道。

1394
00:57:43.930 --> 00:57:46.250
You should get a beeper and a landline just like me.
你应该像我一样买个寻呼机和座机。

1395
00:57:46.390 --> 00:57:46.770
Yeah.
没错。

1396
00:57:46.870 --> 00:57:51.410
Because then you'll know my location if I'm at home and you can't frame me for a crime.
因为那样的话，如果我在家，你就知道我的位置，你就没法陷害我犯罪了。

1397
00:57:51.610 --> 00:57:52.190
That's right.
说得对。

1398
00:57:52.290 --> 00:57:58.810
And if someone really needs to get a hold of you, they can call you and type something in for your beeper.
如果有人真的需要联系你，他们可以打给你，然后在寻呼机上输入信息。

1399
00:57:58.990 --> 00:58:00.270
And then you can read your beeper.
然后你就可以查看寻呼机了。

1400
00:58:00.390 --> 00:58:04.110
And then you can drive to a phone somewhere and call that person back.
接着你可以开车去某个电话亭给那个人回电。

1401
00:58:04.110 --> 00:58:11.990
That sounds convenient and really easy to fit into my lifestyle as I know it today.
听起来很方便，而且确实很容易融入我目前的生活方式。

1402
00:58:12.450 --> 00:58:13.150
All right.
好吧。

1403
00:58:13.290 --> 00:58:14.170
Back on topic.
回到正题。

1404
00:58:14.430 --> 00:58:15.890
Because there's payphones everywhere.
因为到处都是公用电话。

1405
00:58:16.250 --> 00:58:16.450
Not.
才怪。

1406
00:58:16.630 --> 00:58:17.850
There's no payphones anymore.
现在已经没有公用电话了。

1407
00:58:18.130 --> 00:58:19.610
Good luck finding a payphone.
祝你能找到公用电话。

1408
00:58:21.190 --> 00:58:21.770
What?
什么？

1409
00:58:22.110 --> 00:58:22.890
Should we move on?
我们要继续吗？

1410
00:58:23.030 --> 00:58:23.350
Yes.
好的。

1411
00:58:23.490 --> 00:58:23.930
All right.
好吧。

1412
00:58:23.930 --> 00:58:25.230
Next stop.
下一站。

1413
00:58:26.130 --> 00:58:26.670
Pies.
派。

1414
00:58:27.390 --> 00:58:31.530
Kevin is really worried that they are not going to make it on time.
凯文非常担心他们不能准时赶到。

1415
00:58:32.330 --> 00:58:35.790
Laverne closes at 5, which is only 20 minutes from now.
拉文派店5点关门，离现在只有20分钟了。

1416
00:58:36.050 --> 00:58:38.530
Kevin is all of a sudden a math genius.
凯文突然变成了数学天才。

1417
00:58:39.130 --> 00:58:39.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1418
00:58:39.530 --> 00:58:45.610
All of a sudden, Kevin's like, if we drive this fast in this many minutes, then we'll make the pie.
突然间，凯文就像是说，如果我们以这个速度开这么多分钟，就能赶上买派了。

1419
00:58:46.010 --> 00:58:51.430
And Angela's like, wait, you're suddenly you can do math as long as it applies to pies?
安吉拉就说，等等，你突然间只要涉及到派就能做数学题了？

1420
00:58:51.810 --> 00:58:52.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1421
00:58:52.230 --> 00:58:57.030
Oscar switches the scenario and changes it to salad, and then Kevin can't do the math.
奥斯卡把场景换成了沙拉，然后凯文就不会算数了。

1422
00:58:57.210 --> 00:58:58.790
We got fan mail about this.
我们收到了关于这个的粉丝来信。

1423
00:58:58.950 --> 00:59:02.430
First off, we have a compliment from Lizette A.
首先，我们收到来自德克萨斯州休斯顿的莉泽特·A的赞美，她说，

1424
00:59:02.550 --> 00:59:03.950
in Houston, Texas, who says,
她说，

1425
00:59:04.090 --> 00:59:09.470
I love this pie joke from Oscar when he pulls out the calculator and asks Kevin to do math.
我喜欢奥斯卡拿出的计算器让凯文做数学题的那个派的笑话。

1426
00:59:09.690 --> 00:59:11.890
Super smart for whoever wrote that.
写那个段子的人真是太聪明了。

1427
00:59:12.130 --> 00:59:13.450
But Jacob O.
但是来自华盛顿州西雅图的雅各布·O有不同的看法。

1428
00:59:13.630 --> 00:59:15.910
from Seattle, Washington has a counterpoint.
雅各布是一位数学家。

1429
00:59:16.470 --> 00:59:17.950
Jacob is a mathematician.
雅各布是一位数学家。

1430
00:59:18.810 --> 00:59:19.190
Uh-oh.
噢，糟糕。

1431
00:59:19.190 --> 00:59:25.910
Jacob says, this has bothered me for years, and every time I watch this episode, I am irritated by this.
雅各布说，这件事困扰我多年了，每次看这一集，我都会为此感到恼火。

1432
00:59:25.970 --> 00:59:26.410
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1433
00:59:26.410 --> 00:59:36.370
At 13 minutes and 38 seconds, when Oscar asks Kevin, how much is 19,154 pies divided by 61 pies?
在13分38秒时，当奥斯卡问凯文，19154个派除以61个派是多少？

1434
00:59:36.570 --> 00:59:39.750
And Kevin answers, 314 pies.
凯文回答说，314个派。

1435
00:59:40.110 --> 00:59:44.730
While the number is correct, the answer should not be in units of pies.
虽然数字是对的，但答案不应该带“派”这个单位。

1436
00:59:44.730 --> 00:59:49.650
The quotient of two quantities, which have the same units, is unitless.
两个相同单位的量相除，商是没有单位的。

1437
00:59:49.830 --> 00:59:55.470
So the answer is just 314, not 314 pies.
所以答案应该是314，而不是314个派。

1438
00:59:55.950 --> 00:59:58.610
However, Jacob says it gets worse.
然而，雅各布说更糟糕的还在后面。

1439
00:59:58.890 --> 00:59:59.370
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1440
00:59:59.710 --> 01:00:03.490
Pies come with their own canonical division problem.
派有它们自己经典的除法问题。

1441
01:00:04.130 --> 01:00:12.490
Oscar should have asked, how much is 19,154 pies divided among 61 people?
奥斯卡应该问的是，19154个派分给61个人是多少？

1442
01:00:13.010 --> 01:00:13.490
Huh.
嗯。

1443
01:00:14.210 --> 01:00:14.670
Yeah.
是啊。

1444
01:00:14.930 --> 01:00:16.790
Jacob, you've given us a lot to think about.
雅各布，你给了我们很多值得思考的东西。

1445
01:00:17.170 --> 01:00:17.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1446
01:00:17.790 --> 01:00:22.670
Jacob would like to know, why did the writers have Kevin attach the wrong units?
雅各布想知道，为什么编剧要让凯文带上错误的单位？

1447
01:00:22.670 --> 01:00:27.590
Why did they decide to divide pies by pies instead of dividing pies among people?
为什么他们决定用派除以派，而不是把派分给人们？

1448
01:00:28.110 --> 01:00:33.750
Jacob, I can tell you right now, there wasn't a mathematician in that room, and they should have called one.
雅各布，我现在就可以告诉你，编剧室里没有数学家，他们当时应该找一个的。

1449
01:00:33.990 --> 01:00:34.810
Yeah, you're right.
是啊，你说得对。

1450
01:00:34.810 --> 01:00:42.150
But I see Jacob's point, because Oscar is a mathematician, so Oscar would have asked the question correctly.
但我明白雅各布的意思，因为奥斯卡是个数学家，所以奥斯卡本该问出正确的问题。

1451
01:00:42.410 --> 01:00:43.670
He would have phrased it correctly.
他本来会用词准确的。

1452
01:00:43.790 --> 01:00:43.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1453
01:00:44.030 --> 01:00:44.310
Yes.
没错。

1454
01:00:44.450 --> 01:00:44.890
It's true.
确实如此。

1455
01:00:45.050 --> 01:00:46.170
He would have caught that, Jacob.
他本来会发现这一点的，雅各布。

1456
01:00:46.350 --> 01:00:47.230
That was a good catch.
那是个不错的发现。

1457
01:00:47.410 --> 01:00:48.450
It was a good catch.
那确实是个不错的发现。

1458
01:00:48.710 --> 01:00:51.190
Lizette, you are still allowed to love this scene.
莉塞特，你依然可以喜欢这一幕。

1459
01:00:51.590 --> 01:00:54.070
I have a catch for this scene as well.
我对这一幕也有个发现。

1460
01:00:54.190 --> 01:00:55.890
It has nothing to do with mathematics.
这和数学没关系。

1461
01:00:56.430 --> 01:00:58.970
Does it have to do with Meredith's screen?
是和梅雷迪思的屏幕有关吗？

1462
01:00:59.190 --> 01:01:02.850
At 13 minutes and 45 seconds, Kate had been playing solitaire.
在13分45秒时，凯特一直在玩纸牌游戏。

1463
01:01:02.850 --> 01:01:03.810
I saw it, too.
我也看到了。

1464
01:01:03.990 --> 01:01:07.650
I love it that her character is so committed to solitaire.
我很喜欢她这个角色对纸牌游戏如此执着。

1465
01:01:07.890 --> 01:01:11.070
She gets on this work bus and just plays solitaire all day.
她上了这辆工作巴士，然后整天都在玩纸牌。

1466
01:01:11.590 --> 01:01:15.430
Well, now Dwight is going to inform everyone that they're almost out of gas anyway.
好吧，现在德怀特要告诉大家他们快没油了。

1467
01:01:15.850 --> 01:01:21.910
He refuses to get gas, and then he climbs up through the sunroof and is going to go sulk on the top of the bus.
他拒绝去加油，然后爬出天窗，打算去车顶生闷气。

1468
01:01:22.510 --> 01:01:25.990
Because he's on the top of the roof, they now cannot safely drive away.
因为他在车顶上，他们现在没法安全地把车开走。

1469
01:01:26.150 --> 01:01:28.150
Even though Phyllis says just drive away.
尽管菲利斯说直接开走就行。

1470
01:01:28.450 --> 01:01:28.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1471
01:01:29.110 --> 01:01:29.590
Phyllis.
菲利斯。

1472
01:01:30.170 --> 01:01:33.530
Pam is now going to say, Jim, just go check on him.
帕姆现在要说，吉姆，去看看他吧。

1473
01:01:33.770 --> 01:01:34.930
Just something's up.
肯定出什么事了。

1474
01:01:35.050 --> 01:01:35.730
Go check on him.
去看看他。

1475
01:01:36.070 --> 01:01:40.990
Yeah, you know, in the table read draft of this episode, when we all sat down to read this as a cast,
是啊，你知道吗，在这一集的剧本围读稿里，当我们全剧组坐下来读剧本时，

1476
01:01:41.170 --> 01:01:43.270
this was actually a scene between Dwight and Pam.
这其实是德怀特和帕姆之间的一场戏。

1477
01:01:43.590 --> 01:01:46.390
Pam was going to go up on the roof and check on Dwight.
原本是帕姆要上车顶去看看德怀特。

1478
01:01:46.650 --> 01:01:53.530
But after the table read, we had a big discussion about how we thought that it might play better as a Jim Dwight moment.
但在围读之后，我们进行了深入讨论，觉得如果改成吉姆和德怀特的互动效果会更好。

1479
01:01:53.750 --> 01:01:55.170
I agree with that, actually.
说实话，我同意这一点。

1480
01:01:55.170 --> 01:01:56.090
I do, too.
我也同意。

1481
01:01:56.410 --> 01:02:01.710
This is something I haven't shared yet, but since me, John, Rain, and Ed were producers this season,
这件事我还没分享过，但因为我和约翰、雷恩还有埃德这一季担任制片人，

1482
01:02:01.930 --> 01:02:06.550
something that we now did was we would stay after the table reads for the notes sessions.
我们现在会做的一件事就是围读结束后留下来参加剧本研讨会。

1483
01:02:06.850 --> 01:02:07.050
Yeah.
没错。

1484
01:02:07.050 --> 01:02:16.130
And so this was something I remembered was that, oh, yeah, it was decided in the notes session that this would change from Dwight and Pam to Dwight and Jim.
所以我记得就是在那次研讨会上决定把这一幕从德怀特和帕姆改成德怀特和吉姆的。

1485
01:02:16.790 --> 01:02:17.570
Oh, oh!
噢，噢！

1486
01:02:18.070 --> 01:02:22.490
Also, before we go on the roof, Angela, I have to note, at the end of this scene,
另外，在去车顶之前，安吉拉，我必须提一下，在这一幕的结尾，

1487
01:02:23.010 --> 01:02:29.070
Andy's really mad that they're not going to get pie because it probably means he's not going to get banana cream because it's the first to go.
安迪非常生气，因为他们吃不到派了，这可能意味着他吃不到香蕉奶油派了，因为那是第一个被抢光的。

1488
01:02:29.250 --> 01:02:29.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1489
01:02:29.490 --> 01:02:31.230
And then he swishes his curtain.
然后他拉上了帘子。

1490
01:02:31.570 --> 01:02:31.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1491
01:02:31.990 --> 01:02:34.170
It's the same as the one in our studio.
和我们演播室里的那个一模一样。

1492
01:02:34.590 --> 01:02:35.710
Oh, the same shower curtain.
噢，一样的浴帘。

1493
01:02:35.710 --> 01:02:37.110
It looks exactly the same.
看起来完全一样。

1494
01:02:37.270 --> 01:02:42.670
It's like a shower curtain on the top and the bottom, but then in the middle, it's like a plastic see-through thing.
它上下是浴帘材质，但中间有一块透明的塑料部分。

1495
01:02:42.830 --> 01:02:43.730
A clear patch.
一块透明区域。

1496
01:02:43.730 --> 01:02:50.190
So, everybody, if you wonder what our shower curtain thing looks like in our studio, it looks like what Andy has on the work bus.
所以大家，如果你们好奇我们演播室里的浴帘是什么样的，它就和安迪在工作巴士上用的那个一样。

1497
01:02:50.270 --> 01:02:50.710
You know what?
你知道吗？

1498
01:02:50.810 --> 01:02:52.010
I'm going to do a side-by-side.
我要做一个对比图。

1499
01:02:52.210 --> 01:02:52.910
Oh, great.
噢，太棒了。

1500
01:02:53.610 --> 01:02:59.790
I wanted to tell you guys that this heart-to-heart that Jim and Dwight have on top of the bus was much longer in the shooting draft.
我想告诉大家，吉姆和德怀特在车顶上的那次交心，在拍摄剧本里要长得多。

1501
01:03:00.170 --> 01:03:03.290
And let me tell you, Jim really lays into Dwight.
我跟你说，吉姆真的把德怀特骂惨了。

1502
01:03:03.950 --> 01:03:05.170
This is how it was written.
剧本就是这么写的。

1503
01:03:05.570 --> 01:03:07.330
Jim climbs up on top of the roof.
吉姆爬到了车顶上。

1504
01:03:07.570 --> 01:03:08.950
He gently says,
他轻声说道，

1505
01:03:09.450 --> 01:03:09.850
Dwight?
德怀特？

1506
01:03:10.090 --> 01:03:10.490
Dwight.
德怀特。

1507
01:03:10.630 --> 01:03:10.970
Yeah.
嗯。

1508
01:03:11.610 --> 01:03:12.430
Jim says,
吉姆说，

1509
01:03:13.330 --> 01:03:14.950
Why do you have to be such a cheap prick?
你为什么非要这么抠门小气？

1510
01:03:15.530 --> 01:03:21.470
You've got four sources of income, a farm, a bed and breakfast, your job, and you own the building.
你有四份收入来源，农场、民宿、你的工作，而且你还是这栋楼的房东。

1511
01:03:21.690 --> 01:03:23.370
You've got no dependents.
你又没有家属要养。

1512
01:03:23.510 --> 01:03:28.970
I spend every penny on freaking diapers, and all I wanted was to buy my wife a pie.
我把每一分钱都花在那些该死的尿布上了，我不过就是想给我老婆买个派。

1513
01:03:29.390 --> 01:03:32.290
With everything you've got, you couldn't throw me a little bone?
以你现在的身家，就不能稍微帮我一把吗？

1514
01:03:33.190 --> 01:03:33.710
Wow.
哇。

1515
01:03:34.150 --> 01:03:34.670
I know.
我知道。

1516
01:03:34.670 --> 01:03:36.210
He calls him a cheap prick.
他骂他是抠门小气鬼。

1517
01:03:36.650 --> 01:03:38.150
Dwight responds and says,
德怀特回应说，

1518
01:03:38.150 --> 01:03:42.650
Hey, idiot, you're the one who's rich, and you don't even appreciate it.
嘿，白痴，有钱的人是你，而且你根本不懂得珍惜。

1519
01:03:42.950 --> 01:03:43.990
I'm barren.
我不孕不育。

1520
01:03:44.490 --> 01:03:47.570
And then Jim says, what?
然后吉姆说，什么？

1521
01:03:47.750 --> 01:03:49.710
And the scene continues as it aired.
接着剧情就按播出时的那样继续发展。

1522
01:03:49.910 --> 01:03:51.930
And then Jim tells him that was a prank.
然后吉姆告诉他那只是个恶作剧。

1523
01:03:52.650 --> 01:03:52.970
Yes.
没错。

1524
01:03:53.190 --> 01:03:58.310
And then Dwight says, well, prank or no prank, I'm still barren.
然后德怀特说，好吧，不管是不是恶作剧，我还是不孕不育。

1525
01:03:58.830 --> 01:03:59.230
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1526
01:03:59.690 --> 01:04:05.930
Well, Steve Burgess said it was kind of complicated to shoot these two guys up on the top of a bus, as you can imagine.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，如你所想，拍摄这两个人在巴士顶上的戏份相当复杂。

1527
01:04:06.330 --> 01:04:12.770
They had rain harnessed to the top of the bus, but they couldn't harness in John because he had to climb up and move around.
他们给巴士顶部装了安全绳，但没法给约翰装，因为他得爬来爬去。

1528
01:04:13.370 --> 01:04:24.070
So John's just walking around on top of a bus, and then they had our camera operators, Matt and Sarah, were up on ladders to make them as high as the bus.
所以约翰就在巴士顶上走来走去，然后我们的摄影师马特和莎拉站在梯子上，好让他们的视角和巴士顶一样高。

1529
01:04:24.510 --> 01:04:25.670
Very tricky shot.
非常棘手的镜头。

1530
01:04:25.890 --> 01:04:29.970
Well, we learned a little bit of that kind of on top of the bus footage and speed.
我们从那种巴士顶部的拍摄和速度上学到了不少东西。

1531
01:04:30.190 --> 01:04:31.070
We sure did.
确实学到了。

1532
01:04:31.510 --> 01:04:39.990
If you are going to shoot anything on a bus or on top of a bus, you might want to give us a call because we can help you map it out.
如果你打算在巴士上或巴士顶上拍摄任何东西，你可能想给我们打个电话，因为我们可以帮你规划一下。

1533
01:04:40.130 --> 01:04:40.790
We sure can.
我们确实可以。

1534
01:04:41.610 --> 01:04:45.570
Well, Nellie and Erin have finished her adoption forMs.
内莉和艾琳填好了领养表格。

1535
01:04:46.390 --> 01:04:49.910
Nellie's going to walk up to Andy and ask him to sign it for her.
内莉走过去找安迪，请他帮她签字。

1536
01:04:50.270 --> 01:04:54.650
And he says it's unsignable, and he wishes her luck with her impossible dream.
他说这根本没法签，还祝她那个不可能实现的梦想好运。

1537
01:04:55.670 --> 01:04:59.870
Erin watches all of this, and it really hits her hard.
艾琳目睹了这一切，深受打击。

1538
01:05:00.250 --> 01:05:00.690
Yeah.
是啊。

1539
01:05:01.070 --> 01:05:09.690
We're going to hear some crying at the front of the bus, and Andy assumes it's Nellie, and he's kind of ready to go shame her about it.
我们会在巴士前部听到哭声，安迪以为是内莉，正准备去羞辱她一番。

1540
01:05:09.870 --> 01:05:12.790
Yeah, he says British women are famously over-emotional.
没错，他说英国女人出了名的情绪化。

1541
01:05:13.090 --> 01:05:18.090
And Pete says it's not Nellie, very pointedly.
皮特非常明确地指出，那不是内莉。

1542
01:05:18.250 --> 01:05:18.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1543
01:05:18.990 --> 01:05:25.370
And it's revealed that it's Erin who's crying, while Nellie consoles her, saying, listen, it's not your fault.
结果发现哭的是艾琳，内莉在安慰她，说，听着，这不是你的错。

1544
01:05:25.810 --> 01:05:27.110
It's not your fault.
这不是你的错。

1545
01:05:27.670 --> 01:05:34.030
Brent shared with us a little bit about this scene and about how they filmed Nellie crying, and we want you to hear it.
布伦特和我们分享了一些关于这场戏以及他们如何拍摄内莉哭泣的细节，我们想让你听听。

1546
01:05:34.890 --> 01:05:38.190
There's a scene at the end of Work Bus where Nellie Kemper has to cry.
在《工作巴士》这一集的结尾，有一场内莉·肯珀需要哭泣的戏。

1547
01:05:38.190 --> 01:05:46.310
I was on set with Bryan Cranston when Nellie came up to him and said, hey, I just want you to know, as an actress, I cannot cry on cue.
当时我和布莱恩·科兰斯顿在片场，内莉走过来对他说，嘿，我只想让你知道，作为一名演员，我没法说哭就哭。

1548
01:05:46.310 --> 01:05:49.930
And Bryan said to her, it's actually a lot easier than you think.
布莱恩对她说，其实这比你想象的要容易得多。

1549
01:05:49.970 --> 01:05:59.050
And he told her about how he had been a soap opera actor on this show Loving in the 1980s, and he would see the soap opera actresses when they had to cry in a scene.
他告诉她，他在80年代曾是肥皂剧《相爱》的演员，他经常看到那些女演员在需要拍哭戏时是怎么做的。

1550
01:05:59.050 --> 01:06:08.490
They would drink two liters of water in the morning, and Bryan said that if you were hyper-hydrated and you just got sad, the water would pour out of your eyes.
她们会在早上喝两升水，布莱恩说，如果你处于过度补水状态，只要你感到难过，眼泪就会夺眶而出。

1551
01:06:08.950 --> 01:06:21.430
Now, I don't know if Nellie took his advice, and I don't know if she cries real tears in that scene, but if she did, it's the first time Nellie Kemper ever cried on camera.
我不知道内莉是否听取了他的建议，也不知道她在那个场景里流的是不是真眼泪，但如果她流了，那将是内莉·肯珀第一次在镜头前落泪。

1552
01:06:21.430 --> 01:06:25.910
And it's all thanks to Bryan Cranston and the soap opera actresses of Loving.
这一切都要归功于布莱恩·科兰斯顿和《相爱》剧组的肥皂剧女演员们。

1553
01:06:26.910 --> 01:06:31.270
Well, Ange, I traded some text messages with Nellie Kemper about this.
嗯，安吉，我为此和内莉·肯珀发过几条短信。

1554
01:06:31.570 --> 01:06:32.650
What did she say?
她怎么说？

1555
01:06:32.850 --> 01:06:33.790
Is that why she peed?
她尿急是因为这个吗？

1556
01:06:33.850 --> 01:06:35.390
Because she was drinking so much water all day?
是因为她整天都在喝水吗？

1557
01:06:35.770 --> 01:06:36.910
She had a full bladder.
她当时憋了一肚子尿。

1558
01:06:37.310 --> 01:06:39.710
She said she did not take this advice.
她说她没有听取那个建议。

1559
01:06:39.990 --> 01:06:42.150
Oh, she used a menthol stick.
哦，她用了薄荷棒。

1560
01:06:42.490 --> 01:06:44.130
Oh, well, that will make your eyes water.
哦，那确实会让眼睛流泪。

1561
01:06:44.330 --> 01:06:45.210
I've used them.
我用过那个。

1562
01:06:45.410 --> 01:06:49.510
It's like they dab menthol up by your eyes, and it makes them water.
就像是在眼睛附近涂点薄荷膏，眼睛就会流泪。

1563
01:06:49.510 --> 01:06:57.610
And then you just kind of with your voice, and then the menthol does the tears.
然后你只要稍微配合一下声音，薄荷膏就会起到催泪的效果。

1564
01:06:57.950 --> 01:07:01.670
Kenneth Paul, who did my makeup on the show, once asked me if I was a vampire.
肯尼斯·保罗，我在剧组时的化妆师，曾问过我是不是吸血鬼。

1565
01:07:02.290 --> 01:07:02.770
Why?
为什么？

1566
01:07:02.770 --> 01:07:07.570
Because he put the menthol in the corner of my eyes, and my eyes didn't react to it at all.
因为他把薄荷膏涂在我眼角，我的眼睛却一点反应都没有。

1567
01:07:07.890 --> 01:07:09.330
Do vampires not cry?
吸血鬼不会哭吗？

1568
01:07:09.490 --> 01:07:10.270
I don't know.
我不知道。

1569
01:07:10.650 --> 01:07:13.670
He just was like, are you the walking dead?
他当时就问，你是行尸走肉吗？

1570
01:07:14.110 --> 01:07:18.770
He said, I've never seen anyone not have a reaction to the menthol stick.
他说，我从没见过谁对薄荷棒一点反应都没有。

1571
01:07:18.770 --> 01:07:20.670
Do your eyes water when you cut onions?
你切洋葱的时候眼睛会流泪吗？

1572
01:07:21.350 --> 01:07:21.750
Yes.
会。

1573
01:07:22.070 --> 01:07:23.150
Oh, I know.
哦，我知道了。

1574
01:07:23.290 --> 01:07:26.770
So maybe that's how we make you cry in your next project.
也许这就是我们让你在下一个项目中哭出来的方法。

1575
01:07:27.070 --> 01:07:29.190
I guess I'm going to have to roll in with a bunch of onions.
看来我得带着一堆洋葱去片场了。

1576
01:07:29.470 --> 01:07:30.890
I love this visual.
我喜欢这个画面。

1577
01:07:31.310 --> 01:07:32.470
I love this idea.
我喜欢这个主意。

1578
01:07:32.990 --> 01:07:36.030
If I get a job on a soap opera, I'm like, one second, let me chop an onion.
如果我接了一部肥皂剧，我会说，等一下，让我先切个洋葱。

1579
01:07:36.850 --> 01:07:41.970
Jim is going to convince Dwight that he has a lot of children, and they are his work children.
吉姆打算让德怀特相信他有很多孩子，而且是他的“工作孩子”。

1580
01:07:41.970 --> 01:07:43.430
They are his bildenkinder.
也就是他的“工作子女”。

1581
01:07:43.430 --> 01:07:48.470
And there's something he can do for his bildenkinder, and it's get them some pie.
他能为他的“工作子女”做点什么呢，那就是给他们买点派。

1582
01:07:49.410 --> 01:07:49.610
Yep.
没错。

1583
01:07:50.270 --> 01:07:51.930
Dwight is inspired by this.
德怀特深受启发。

1584
01:07:52.150 --> 01:07:54.750
We did have a tiny catch from Allison Y.
我们确实收到了来自肯塔基州路易斯维尔的艾莉森·Y的一条小发现。

1585
01:07:54.930 --> 01:07:58.370
in Louisville, Kentucky, who said, I've been waiting for this.
她说，我等这个很久了。

1586
01:07:58.370 --> 01:07:59.930
Little background catch.
一个背景小发现。

1587
01:08:00.150 --> 01:08:08.650
The office staff are upset that the pie stand closes at 5, and it's already 442 when Jim climbs onto the roof to go after Dwight.
办公室员工对派摊下午5点关门感到不满，而当吉姆爬上屋顶去追德怀特时，时间已经是4点42分了。

1588
01:08:08.990 --> 01:08:14.350
However, if you look at the watch on Jim's wrist, it actually says 255.
然而，如果你看吉姆手腕上的手表，时间其实是2点55分。

1589
01:08:14.790 --> 01:08:15.690
It's true.
是真的。

1590
01:08:15.950 --> 01:08:27.250
You can see Jim's watch very clearly at 15 minutes, 42 seconds, 17 minutes, 24 seconds, and the best shot of it is at 18 minutes, 2 seconds, and it is 255.
你可以在15分42秒、17分24秒清楚地看到吉姆的手表，最清晰的镜头是在18分02秒，显示时间是2点55分。

1591
01:08:27.250 --> 01:08:38.770
Well, here it is, folks, our almost death number one, when Dwight comes down from the roof and gets behind the wheel and starts speeding away toward the pie.
好了，各位，这就是我们的“准死亡”第一名，当时德怀特从屋顶下来，坐进驾驶座，开始加速冲向派摊。

1592
01:08:39.010 --> 01:08:40.130
Where do we even start?
我们该从哪里说起呢？

1593
01:08:40.470 --> 01:08:45.890
First of all, we rehearsed the scene, and Rain was actually going to be pretending to drive, but not driving.
首先，我们排练过这个场景，雷恩本来是要假装开车，而不是真的在开。

1594
01:08:46.150 --> 01:08:48.910
Yeah, the bus was hooked up to a pull rig.
没错，巴士是用拖车装置拉着的。

1595
01:08:49.070 --> 01:08:49.430
Yes.
是的。

1596
01:08:49.430 --> 01:08:57.070
And off camera, they were going to yell, swerve right, and the whole cast would all lurch to the right.
在镜头外，他们会喊“向右急转”，然后全体演员都要向右倾斜。

1597
01:08:57.270 --> 01:08:59.210
Then they'd say, swerve left.
然后他们会喊“向左急转”。

1598
01:08:59.230 --> 01:09:00.770
We'd all lurch to the left.
我们就全体向左倾斜。

1599
01:09:01.190 --> 01:09:03.530
But, in fact, we were just driving along straight.
但实际上，我们只是在平稳地直线行驶。

1600
01:09:03.790 --> 01:09:04.090
Yes.
是的。

1601
01:09:04.470 --> 01:09:05.930
And we were not even driving.
而且我们当时甚至都没在开车。

1602
01:09:06.110 --> 01:09:06.970
We were being pulled.
我们是被拖着走的。

1603
01:09:07.150 --> 01:09:07.410
Correct.
没错。

1604
01:09:07.410 --> 01:09:07.870
Very safe.
非常安全。

1605
01:09:07.970 --> 01:09:08.590
Very safe.
非常安全。

1606
01:09:08.750 --> 01:09:09.030
Yes.
是的。

1607
01:09:09.450 --> 01:09:11.870
Well, they watched that in playback, and guess what?
结果他们回看录像时，你猜怎么着？

1608
01:09:11.950 --> 01:09:12.950
It looked real phony.
看起来特别假。

1609
01:09:13.310 --> 01:09:14.310
Super fakey.
超级假。

1610
01:09:14.310 --> 01:09:19.710
We didn't do a really good job, I guess, of fake swerving, so they said, you know what?
我想我们假装转弯演得不够好，所以他们说，你知道吗？

1611
01:09:19.770 --> 01:09:21.950
We're going to take the bus off the rig.
我们要把巴士从拖车上卸下来。

1612
01:09:22.090 --> 01:09:23.910
We're going to put a stunt driver in.
我们要换个特技车手来开。

1613
01:09:24.190 --> 01:09:25.390
Rain, you hop out.
Rain，你下去。

1614
01:09:25.830 --> 01:09:32.010
Now we're going to drive down the road, and when we yell, swerve right, the stunt driver is going to swerve right.
现在我们要开车上路了，当我们喊向右转时，特技车手就会向右转。

1615
01:09:32.170 --> 01:09:36.090
Yeah, and we should just naturally react.
对，然后我们只要做出自然的反应就行了。

1616
01:09:36.670 --> 01:09:36.850
Right.
没错。

1617
01:09:36.850 --> 01:09:46.250
What no one thought about was that there were hundreds of items inside a tiny bus, and all of them were not nailed down.
没人想到的是，那辆小巴士里有几百件物品，而且它们都没被钉死。

1618
01:09:46.450 --> 01:09:47.870
They weren't tied down.
它们都没被固定住。

1619
01:09:48.190 --> 01:09:50.350
Everything you see was loose.
你看到的一切都是松动的。

1620
01:09:50.590 --> 01:09:56.490
Rolling chairs, desks, lamps, staplers, water cooler, coffee pot.
转椅、桌子、台灯、订书机、饮水机、咖啡壶。

1621
01:09:56.750 --> 01:10:00.550
None of it was taped down, nailed down, strapped down.
没有一样东西是用胶带粘住、钉死或绑住的。

1622
01:10:00.810 --> 01:10:01.390
None of it.
一样都没有。

1623
01:10:01.590 --> 01:10:04.650
And literally no one thought of this.
真的没人想到这一点。

1624
01:10:04.870 --> 01:10:05.830
None of us.
我们谁也没想到。

1625
01:10:05.830 --> 01:10:07.290
I don't know what was up.
我不知道当时是怎么回事。

1626
01:10:07.450 --> 01:10:16.690
And then we start off down the road, and when they told the stunt driver to swerve, he swerved like I thought the bus was going to tip over.
然后我们开始上路，当他们告诉特技车手转弯时，他转得猛到我以为巴士要翻了。

1627
01:10:16.830 --> 01:10:18.610
It was like such a hard turn.
那转弯实在太猛了。

1628
01:10:18.890 --> 01:10:27.970
It was so intense, and the entire cast and all of the contents of the bus went flying into the side of the bus.
太激烈了，整个剧组人员和巴士里的所有东西都飞向了巴士的一侧。

1629
01:10:28.150 --> 01:10:32.190
And you can see it in real time because that's the take we used.
你可以实时看到那一幕，因为那就是我们采用的镜头。

1630
01:10:32.190 --> 01:10:39.890
They used a very tiny portion of the take because we were on the floor covered in things.
他们只用了那个镜头里很小的一部分，因为我们当时都倒在地上，身上盖满了东西。

1631
01:10:40.070 --> 01:10:40.910
Covered in people.
身上盖满了人。

1632
01:10:41.110 --> 01:10:41.890
Covered in people.
身上盖满了人。

1633
01:10:42.070 --> 01:10:43.850
You couldn't even see Creed.
你甚至都看不到Creed了。

1634
01:10:43.850 --> 01:10:45.970
He was covered with so many things.
他被太多东西盖住了。

1635
01:10:46.070 --> 01:10:46.570
And people.
还有人。

1636
01:10:46.630 --> 01:10:47.070
And people.
还有人。

1637
01:10:47.070 --> 01:10:50.570
I hurt my knee because who was it?
我膝盖受伤了，因为那是谁的？

1638
01:10:50.690 --> 01:10:51.590
Was it Clark's chair?
是Clark的椅子吗？

1639
01:10:51.790 --> 01:10:52.690
Rolled into my chair.
滚到了我的椅子上。

1640
01:10:52.850 --> 01:10:53.190
I rolled.
我滚开了。

1641
01:10:53.450 --> 01:10:53.950
Everything.
所有东西。

1642
01:10:53.950 --> 01:10:55.970
I got smooshed up against the wall.
我被挤在墙上。

1643
01:10:56.170 --> 01:10:57.310
Everything rolled into me.
所有东西都滚到了我身上。

1644
01:10:57.570 --> 01:10:57.850
Yes.
是的。

1645
01:10:57.850 --> 01:10:59.990
My lamp slid into my lap.
我的台灯滑到了我的腿上。

1646
01:11:00.130 --> 01:11:02.190
I remember catching my lamp in my lap.
我记得我用腿接住了我的台灯。

1647
01:11:02.510 --> 01:11:02.770
Yeah.
没错。

1648
01:11:02.790 --> 01:11:04.550
I was on the ground.
我当时倒在地上。

1649
01:11:04.730 --> 01:11:06.270
Leslie was on top of me.
Leslie压在我身上。

1650
01:11:06.410 --> 01:11:11.150
And I remember we had to pull a lot of things out to find Phyllis.
我记得我们不得不搬开很多东西才找到Phyllis。

1651
01:11:11.330 --> 01:11:12.510
She hurt her ankle.
她扭伤了脚踝。

1652
01:11:12.830 --> 01:11:14.590
Our camera operators.
我们的摄像师们。

1653
01:11:14.770 --> 01:11:15.050
Yes.
是的。

1654
01:11:15.130 --> 01:11:15.890
They went flying.
他们飞了出去。

1655
01:11:15.950 --> 01:11:18.230
They went flying while holding cameras.
他们抱着摄像机飞了出去。

1656
01:11:18.490 --> 01:11:19.330
80-pound cameras.
80磅重的摄像机。

1657
01:11:19.570 --> 01:11:19.990
Yes.
没错。

1658
01:11:20.150 --> 01:11:27.130
And true to their love of their cameras and the equipment, you know, they used their bodies to shield the cameras.
出于对摄像机和器材的热爱，你知道，他们用自己的身体护住了摄像机。

1659
01:11:27.130 --> 01:11:30.150
The bus was an absolute mess.
巴士里简直乱成了一团。

1660
01:11:30.310 --> 01:11:34.970
It was like someone picked it up and shook it in the air and everything went everywhere.
就像有人把它拎起来在空中摇晃，所有东西都散落得到处都是。

1661
01:11:35.790 --> 01:11:38.050
I mean, I'm thinking back to it.
我是说，回想起来。

1662
01:11:38.610 --> 01:11:42.530
We stopped the bus and we were just in a daze.
我们停下巴士，整个人都懵了。

1663
01:11:42.790 --> 01:11:43.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1664
01:11:43.350 --> 01:11:45.350
We got off the side of the road.
我们从路边下了车。

1665
01:11:45.490 --> 01:11:46.850
I don't even remember where we were.
我甚至不记得我们在哪儿。

1666
01:11:47.030 --> 01:11:51.430
We couldn't even get off very quickly because they had to, like, kind of pull us out of it all.
我们甚至没法很快下车，因为他们得把我们从那堆乱七八糟的东西里拉出来。

1667
01:11:51.670 --> 01:11:52.030
Yes.
是的。

1668
01:11:52.290 --> 01:11:54.270
The medics came rushing up.
医护人员匆忙赶来。

1669
01:11:54.270 --> 01:12:01.530
We were able to assess that everyone was, you know, had bumps and bruises but were ultimately okay.
我们评估了一下，每个人都受了点磕碰和淤青，但最终都没什么大碍。

1670
01:12:02.610 --> 01:12:06.030
But shook up, I think, is a fair assessment.
但我觉得用“惊魂未定”来形容很贴切。

1671
01:12:06.630 --> 01:12:09.270
There were some bathrooms nearby.
附近有一些洗手间。

1672
01:12:09.270 --> 01:12:11.750
We were, like, in a random park.
我们当时就在一个随处可见的公园里。

1673
01:12:11.950 --> 01:12:12.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1674
01:12:12.510 --> 01:12:17.130
And I remember there were, like, these hikers coming back from a hike.
我记得当时有几个徒步旅行者刚回来。

1675
01:12:17.130 --> 01:12:26.710
Like, I just remember the look on their face because they were just watching the cast of The Office walking in a daze to the public restroom.
我记得他们脸上的表情，因为他们看着《办公室》的演员们神情恍惚地走向公共厕所。

1676
01:12:27.170 --> 01:12:28.770
I went in there with Phyllis.
我和菲利斯一起进去了。

1677
01:12:28.990 --> 01:12:31.030
They got ice for Phyllis, I remember.
我记得他们给菲利斯拿了冰块。

1678
01:12:31.250 --> 01:12:31.470
Yep.
没错。

1679
01:12:31.790 --> 01:12:33.310
My knee was a little messed up.
我的膝盖受了点伤。

1680
01:12:33.330 --> 01:12:33.610
Yeah.
是啊。

1681
01:12:33.910 --> 01:12:35.090
We couldn't believe it.
我们简直不敢相信。

1682
01:12:35.230 --> 01:12:36.190
We were like, wow.
我们当时想，哇。

1683
01:12:36.810 --> 01:12:37.250
Wow.
哇。

1684
01:12:37.450 --> 01:12:38.310
That just happened.
刚才竟然发生了这种事。

1685
01:12:38.630 --> 01:12:39.070
Yes.
是的。

1686
01:12:39.490 --> 01:12:42.690
They had to reset the whole interior of the bus.
他们不得不重新布置巴士的整个内部。

1687
01:12:42.830 --> 01:12:42.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1688
01:12:43.010 --> 01:12:44.010
We took a lunch break.
我们休息吃了午饭。

1689
01:12:44.190 --> 01:12:44.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1690
01:12:44.350 --> 01:12:45.290
We were like, forget it.
我们当时想，算了吧。

1691
01:12:45.370 --> 01:12:46.250
Let's go to lunch.
去吃午饭吧。

1692
01:12:46.470 --> 01:12:50.810
And we couldn't even ride back to our base camp in the bus, which had been the intention.
而且我们甚至没法坐那辆巴士回大本营了，原本是打算坐那辆车的。

1693
01:12:50.810 --> 01:12:52.310
So they had to bring all these vans.
所以他们不得不叫来所有这些面包车。

1694
01:12:52.670 --> 01:12:53.770
But we got back.
但我们还是回去了。

1695
01:12:53.770 --> 01:12:54.830
We had lunch.
我们吃了午饭。

1696
01:12:55.410 --> 01:12:56.490
We were like, we're okay.
我们当时想，我们没事。

1697
01:12:56.730 --> 01:12:58.390
We kind of ended up laughing about it.
最后我们反而笑了起来。

1698
01:12:58.430 --> 01:12:59.930
We were like, oh, my God, that's crazy.
我们当时说，天哪，这太疯狂了。

1699
01:13:00.010 --> 01:13:03.510
We're like, Brian Cranston, you almost killed the whole cast of The Office.
我们说，布莱恩·克兰斯顿，你差点杀了《办公室》的所有演员。

1700
01:13:03.710 --> 01:13:04.810
Ha, ha, ha, ha.
哈哈哈哈。

1701
01:13:05.050 --> 01:13:06.230
But we're okay.
但我们没事的。

1702
01:13:06.230 --> 01:13:06.990
Yes.
是的。

1703
01:13:07.210 --> 01:13:11.970
And, you know, he had had a number of crazy things happen on that RV in Breaking Bad where
而且，你知道，他在《绝命毒师》里的那辆房车上经历过很多疯狂的事，

1704
01:13:11.970 --> 01:13:16.510
it's like, you know, going back and forth and all of the meth lab is flying all over
比如，你知道，车子来回晃动，整个冰毒实验室的东西到处乱飞，

1705
01:13:16.510 --> 01:13:16.890
the place.
到处都是。

1706
01:13:17.030 --> 01:13:19.150
So we're just trading crazy stories.
所以我们当时就在交换彼此的疯狂故事。

1707
01:13:19.470 --> 01:13:20.570
He felt really bad, though.
不过他当时感觉很愧疚。

1708
01:13:20.770 --> 01:13:20.950
He did.
确实是。

1709
01:13:21.070 --> 01:13:21.990
He was so sweet.
他真是太贴心了。

1710
01:13:22.110 --> 01:13:25.750
I mean, we cannot express enough how sweet Brian Cranston is.
我是说，我们怎么夸布莱恩·科兰斯顿的贴心都不为过。

1711
01:13:26.470 --> 01:13:27.450
But it was right.
但那是对的。

1712
01:13:27.610 --> 01:13:28.510
We're like, it's fine.
我们当时就说，没关系的。

1713
01:13:28.850 --> 01:13:29.570
It's fine.
没关系。

1714
01:13:29.930 --> 01:13:33.590
And after lunch, we had some more scenes to shoot on the bus.
午饭后，我们还要在车上拍几场戏。

1715
01:13:33.590 --> 01:13:38.510
They had gotten it all put back together, and they brought us together, and they said,
他们已经把车修好了，把我们叫到一起，然后说，

1716
01:13:38.570 --> 01:13:42.250
guys, we're so sorry about what happened, but we have kind of an exciting announcement.
伙计们，对于刚才发生的事我们深感抱歉，但我们有个令人兴奋的消息要宣布。

1717
01:13:42.590 --> 01:13:48.210
We know it's just been hot and miserable on this bus, but we have found a portable air
我们知道在这辆车上又热又难受，但我们找来了一台便携式空调。

1718
01:13:48.210 --> 01:13:49.130
conditioning unit.
空调机。

1719
01:13:49.510 --> 01:13:52.570
Yeah, we could hook it up to the back of the bus.
对，我们可以把它连在车尾。

1720
01:13:52.770 --> 01:13:56.630
We're going to like tow it on like a little trailer behind us.
我们打算用后面的一辆小拖车把它拖着走。

1721
01:13:56.870 --> 01:14:01.290
And it'll have a tube that comes in the top vent, and it's silent.
它会有一根管子通向车顶的通风口，而且它是静音的。

1722
01:14:01.290 --> 01:14:05.470
Yeah, we can keep it on the whole shoot, the whole rest of the day.
没错，我们可以让它在拍摄期间一直开着，直到今天结束。

1723
01:14:05.910 --> 01:14:06.390
Amazing.
太棒了。

1724
01:14:06.850 --> 01:14:07.850
Yes, it's clean.
是的，很清爽。

1725
01:14:07.850 --> 01:14:10.190
We don't have any more crazy driving stunts.
我们再也没有疯狂的驾驶特技了。

1726
01:14:10.350 --> 01:14:14.430
We're just going to drive and capture the last few scenes.
我们只需要开车，然后拍完最后几场戏。

1727
01:14:14.790 --> 01:14:15.830
It's going to be great.
这会很棒的。

1728
01:14:16.410 --> 01:14:17.550
It's so excited.
太让人兴奋了。

1729
01:14:17.690 --> 01:14:18.170
